 "description": "Where a wallet's USDC on Base came from: every address that sent it USDC, with amounts, transfer counts and block ranges. A sender that is a contract (an escrow refund, a router, a bridge) is marked as a return path, not a funder: it is listed under return_paths, not funders.\nCall it on a line: a call without one has only a moment, enough for a small range of recent blocks, and is cut, uncharged, when it needs longer. from_block is a block number and defaults to the whole history; Base adds about 43,200 blocks a day. The first answer says how many windows the scan will take and about how many milliseconds, at the pace of recent scans, and each one after says how many are done.\n$0.000001 per millisecond on a line.\nPaid, on a line. With no wallet code, ZEAM :: Pass buys the time and opens the line for you, with a pass (https://mcp.zeamprism.com/pass) or your own wallet: https://mcp.zeamprism.com/how-to-pay\nExample: {\"address\":\"0x000000000000000000000000000000000000dEaD\",\"from_block\":51000000}",
 "inputSchema": {
  "examples": [
   {
    "address": "0x000000000000000000000000000000000000dEaD",
    "from_block": 51000000
   }
  ],
  "properties": {
   "address": {
    "description": "string \u2014 the wallet, 0x form.",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "from_block": {
    "description": "optional int \u2014 the block to start from; default the whole history. If the line runs out mid-scan you get what was scanned so far, marked partial; continue with to_block set to one below scanned.from.",
    "minimum": 0,
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "line": {
    "description": "Optional. A line credential, for a client that cannot send the x-line header or _meta[\"zeam-pass/line\"]: the call runs on that line's time.",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "to_block": {
    "description": "optional int \u2014 stop; default the head.",
    "minimum": 0,
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "token": {
    "description": "optional string \u2014 the asset to follow, 0x form; default USDC.",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "window": {
    "description": "optional int \u2014 blocks per snapshot, default 10000; smaller gives a short line its first snapshot sooner.",
    "minimum": 1,
    "type": "integer"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "address"
  ],
  "type": "object"
 },
